### Aura Auth Service - Test Endpoints
### Use la extensión REST Client de VS Code para probar estos endpoints

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1/admin
@adminUserId = 1

### ========== USUARIOS ==========

### 1. Listar todos los usuarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1

### 2. Crear un nuevo usuario
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 3. Crear otro usuario
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "janedoe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "JaneSecure456!",
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 4. Obtener usuario específico (ID = 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2 HTTP/1.1

### 5. Obtener usuario específico (ID = 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/3 HTTP/1.1

### ========== ROLES ==========

### 6. Listar todos los roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles HTTP/1.1

### 7. Crear un nuevo rol
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "editor",
  "description": "Editor de contenido del sistema"
}

### 8. Crear otro rol
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "moderator",
  "description": "Moderador de comunidad"
}

### 9. Obtener rol específico (ID = 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/1 HTTP/1.1

### 10. Obtener rol específico (ID = 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/3 HTTP/1.1

### ========== ASIGNACIÓN DE ROLES ==========

### 11. Asignar rol "editor" a usuario "jdoe" (user_id=2, role_id=3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/assign_role HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 12. Asignar rol "moderator" a usuario "jdoe" (user_id=2, role_id=4)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/assign_role HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 4,
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 13. Asignar rol "admin" a usuario "janedoe" (user_id=3, role_id=1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/3/assign_role HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 1,
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### ========== VALIDACIONES Y ERRORES ==========

### 14. ERROR: Username duplicado
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "email": "another@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 15. ERROR: Email duplicado
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newuser",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 16. ERROR: Password muy corta
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "short",
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 17. ERROR: Usuario no existe
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/9999 HTTP/1.1

### 18. ERROR: Rol no existe (assign_role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/assign_role HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 9999,
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 19. ERROR: Rol ya asignado (intenta asignar dos veces el mismo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/assign_role HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "created_by_id": {{adminUserId}}
}

### 20. ERROR: Rol ya existe
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "admin",
  "description": "Duplicado"
}

### ========== VERIFICACIONES FINALES ==========

### 21. Listar usuarios (para ver roles asignados)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1

### 22. Obtener usuario con roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2 HTTP/1.1

### 23. Obtener usuario 3 con roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/3 HTTP/1.1

### 24. Obtener rol con detalles
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/3 HTTP/1.1
